Subject: [PATCH 2/5] msi: acknowledge before reading channel status

The handler cleared the MSI vector at the very end, after every loop status had been read. A
descriptor completing in between had its notification destroyed by that clear: the status read had
already missed it, and the bit it set was wiped on the way out.

In loop mode this is invisible, because interrupts keep arriving and the next one recomputes the count
from a free running register. In one-shot mode the last interrupt of a batch is the only one that will
ever be sent, so losing it hangs the transfer.

Clearing the latched vector first, and repeating until it reads back empty, means a notification
landing at any point during servicing is picked up rather than lost.

The repeat is bounded. A card that has left the bus reads as all ones, so its vector never reads back
empty, and an open loop would hold the CPU in hard IRQ context for good. All ones ends the handler at
once and any other vector that will not clear ends it after 4 passes.

